WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.068
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.802
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.802 --> 00:00:05.938
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:07.640
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.375
Let's get to some jokes.

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:11.310
Well, guys, tomorrow,
President Biden is giving

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:16.549
a major speech on the next phase
of his pandemic response.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.751
Americans said they
can't wait to hear the speech

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:22.288
and then crowd into a bar
for tomorrow's NFL kickoff.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:28.627
Yeah, Biden wants to stop COVID
before more variants emerge.

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:30.229
He'll be like,
"Either you take this seriously

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:33.066
or you're going to have to learn
the whole Greek alphabet."

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:36.903
That's right --
Biden will lay out

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:40.039
a six-prong strategy
to fight COVID.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.641
And, apparently,
one prong is building

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.010
a border wall between
the U.S. and Florida.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.812
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's all it is.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.446
Just a wall.
♪♪

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:50.650
That's all it is.
-Oh!

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.952
-That's right --
it's a six-prong strategy.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.187
Actually,
it's a six-word strategy --

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:56.756
"Quit it with the horse pills."

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.791
It's interesting.

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:00.360
Pretty soon,
Americans are going to be

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.028
looking at
eight flowcharts like,

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.963
"Alright,
we're on prong number 4,

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:07.834
Code Blue, Stage 7, Level 12.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.269
So we can go to
Applebee's tonight.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:12.906
Okay, we're allowed to do this."

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.708
Meanwhile, after taking a year
off because of the pandemic,

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.910
Macy's announced that
the public will once again

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.345
be able to attend the

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.814
Thanksgiving Day Parade
in New York City.

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:24.017
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, that's right.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.554
That's right --
people will quickly realize

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.623
that standing for three hours
in the freezing cold

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.357
with their kids isn't
the "back to normal"

00:01:32.357 --> 00:01:34.393
they've been missing.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:35.895
It should be pretty safe.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:39.064
I mean, not even COVID wants to
be near 700 volunteer clowns.

00:01:39.064 --> 00:01:40.900
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.673
Hey, I saw this weekend,
former president Trump

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:51.210
is going to do ringside
commentary for a boxing match

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.912
in Florida.

00:01:54.613 --> 00:01:56.782
Even Rudy Giuliani took a break
from Cameo to say,

00:01:56.782 --> 00:02:00.019
"This is kind of sad."

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.855
Yep, Trump is going to do
boxing commentary.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.290
It was like
he wasn't even president

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.391
and his life just picked up

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:08.727
right where it
left off, you know?

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:12.231
The fight is at the Hard Rock
Hotel &amp; Casino in Florida.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.166
It'll be crazy when Trump
walks through the door

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:16.269
and the casino
instantly goes bankrupt.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.304
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:23.275
Well, get this.

00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:24.777
I read that people
here in the U.S.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:29.082
are now spending more time on
TikTok than they are on YouTube.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.217
When they heard,
your parents were like,

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.485
"Oh, come on.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:35.387
We just figured out
how to get on the YouTube."

00:02:35.387 --> 00:02:37.990
That's right --
people are spending more time

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.525
on TikTok than YouTube.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:40.893
It's a pretty big deal.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.962
I mean, when YouTube heard
the news, they were like...

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.731
-[ Bleats loudly ]

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:49.335
-Because YouTube has been
on top for a long time,

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:52.138
but TikTok just kind of waltzed
into the room like...

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.540
-How do democracies respond
to those candidate?

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.275
-And what will it mean for...

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:59.578
-YouTube didn't really see
this coming.

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:01.648
It totally blindsided
them like...

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:04.617
-There goes a couple of plows,
demonstrating --

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:08.721
-Seriously, it hit YouTube out
of nowhere, kind of like...

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:12.492
[ Both screaming ]

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:14.527
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:19.965
But it makes sense that
TikTok is doing well.

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:22.034
I mean, all the dances
are so impressive.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.569
Meanwhile, YouTube is like...

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.605
[ Ray Parker Jr.'s
"Ghostbusters" playing ]

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:31.177
-Long story short, for YouTube,
it's been a really far fall

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.712
from the top, kind of like...

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:40.320
[ Laughs ]

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.922
"Hey, Ron."
"How you doin', Billy?"

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:47.693
-"Hey, Billy."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:50.330
-Like that's remotely normal.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.897
"Hey, Ron."
"How you doing there, Billy?"

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:53.299
-"How's it going?

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.901
You have that
wrench I was looking for?"

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:58.404
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.505
-Some business news.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.873
I saw that,
next year, Whole Foods

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:04.376
will open two stores
without cashiers.

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:05.544
That story again.

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:06.879
Starting next year,

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.882
groceries will be free
at two Whole Foods locations.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.918
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.559
Whole Foods made the call after
they couldn't find a cashier

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:24.263
who could keep a straight face
while ringing up a $9 apple.

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:26.031
"Yeah, sure it's organic, yeah."

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:27.299
This is interesting.

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:30.003
According to a new study,
people spend 100 days

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:34.207
of their lives deciding what
TV shows and movies to watch.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:37.243
Over three months only
to settle on,

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.411
"I'll watch whatever you want

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:42.314
and then quietly stew for
the next two hours."

00:04:42.314 --> 00:04:44.850
And, finally, a 4-year-old girl
named Scarlett

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.320
just climbed her
48th mountain peak.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.422
That's great, but she doesn't
have Instagram,

00:04:50.422 --> 00:04:52.157
so did it really happen?

00:04:52.157 --> 00:04:53.525
We have a great show.

00:04:53.525 --> 00:04:55.494
Give it up for The Roots,
ladies and gentlemen! Come on!

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:57.563
-♪ Design a finer rhyme
that's right on time ♪

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.665
♪ I'm a step beyond,
I'm not behind the line ♪

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:01.033
♪ Separate thought from divine ♪

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.269
♪ Better take it as a caution or
as a warning sign ♪

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.804
♪ The man at hand
that rule the school ♪

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.039
♪ And reach and teach the blind
and find from "A" to "Z" ♪

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.709
♪ And be the most to boast,
I'm loud and proud ♪

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:12.144
♪♪

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:15.013
-Hello, everybody!

00:05:15.013 --> 00:05:17.015
Thank you so much for being --
Before we get started,

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:18.684
just a reminder, the NFL season

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:21.420
kicks off tomorrow night,
right here on NBC.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.522
It is the
Bucs versus the Cowboys.

00:05:23.522 --> 00:05:25.725
And we have a big, big show
right after the game.

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.960
John Cena will be here
in studio.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.994
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:31.197
We'll be doing something
fun with him.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:34.867
Plus, global music superstar
J Balvin will be stopping by.

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:35.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.102
We'll be talking to him,
and he's got

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:38.871
an amazing performance
you don't want to miss.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.806
It's all happening
tomorrow night.

00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:42.775
Set your DVRs.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.276
Tune in, NBC tomorrow night.

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:46.679
But, first, what a show we have
for you tonight.

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:50.249
This Sunday, he and Jon Stewart
are putting on a show called

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:54.753
"NYC Still Rising After
20 Years: A Comedy Celebration"

00:05:54.753 --> 00:05:56.288
at Madison Square Garden.

00:05:56.288 --> 00:05:59.091
Pete Davidson is here tonight!
-Yeah, Peter!

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:00.626
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.428
Come on.
-Dude, he's the --

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:03.462
That's our dude.

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:05.531
-That's our man.

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:09.335
-Plus, she stars in the new film
"Vacation Friends" on Hulu.

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.070
Meredith Hagner is here!

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:14.339
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:14.339 --> 00:06:16.708
And we've got a great in-studio
performance tonight

00:06:16.708 --> 00:06:18.544
from Baby Keem!

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.512
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.512 --> 00:06:23.048
-It's awesome, by the way.

00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:26.318
I saw rehearsals,
and, ooh, man, it's great.

00:06:26.318 --> 00:06:28.421
Guys, do you ever see a photo
in the news and think,

00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:30.489
"That headline could be
much better"?

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:32.825
I'll show you what I mean.
It's time for "News &amp; Improved."

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:34.493
Here we go.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:40.233
-♪ "News &amp; Improved" ♪

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:42.368
-For example,
check out this first photo.

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:43.403
The original headline was...

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:48.241
That headline could definitely
be improved,

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:50.075
because if you
only looked at the photo,

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:51.177
the headline could've been...

00:06:57.082 --> 00:06:58.718
-Chomp!
-You see how this works?

00:06:58.718 --> 00:07:00.153
Alright, let's check out
this next photo.

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.187
The original headline was...

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:05.024
But if you only looked
at the photo,

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:06.325
the headline could've been...

00:07:14.833 --> 00:07:16.135
Up next, this headline says...

00:07:19.471 --> 00:07:20.640
Headline could've been...

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:26.211
"Up top."

00:07:26.211 --> 00:07:27.780
No?

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.115
Next headline was...

00:07:31.683 --> 00:07:32.852
Headline could've been...

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.525
[ Posh English accent ]
Three more beans, please.

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:42.595
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:44.430
-[ Posh English accent ] Yes.
-Thank you.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:48.501
Just three more beans, please.

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:49.735
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:52.038
I'll have his beans, as well.

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:53.105
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:54.373
[ Normal voice ]
This next headline was...

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.512
The headline could've been...

00:08:03.882 --> 00:08:07.152
[ Laughing ]
"How you doing?

00:08:07.152 --> 00:08:09.955
Picked it up earlier."

00:08:09.955 --> 00:08:11.157
Next headline was...

00:08:13.558 --> 00:08:14.827
Headline could've been...

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:21.867
Thousandaire.

00:08:21.867 --> 00:08:23.569
-Thousandaire.

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:25.137
-And, finally,
this headline was...

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.509
Headline could've been...

00:08:32.978 --> 00:08:35.381
That's all the time we have
for "News &amp; Improved."

